## Varying the dose: randomised intensities

Rather than randomising which firms receive the intervention, you can randomise how much of it they receive. For example, some firms might have all eligible employees participate in a training intervention, while others have only half, and others none. Comparing outcomes across these groups reveals not just whether the intervention works but how much of it is needed - and whether the benefits spill over to employees who were not directly treated.

